{2}{y}^{2}-4)(\\sqrt{xy+2}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (2,1)}\\frac{xy-2}{(xy-2)(xy+2)(\\sqrt{xy+2}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (2,1)}\\frac{1}{(xy+2)(\\sqrt{xy+2}+2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (2,1)}\\frac{1}{(xy+2)(\\sqrt{xy+2}+2)} & =\\frac{1}{(2\\cdot 1+2)(\\sqrt{2\\cdot 1+2}+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot 4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $\\frac{1}{16}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407850 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407853 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407850 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "23171e8d-210d-5c2c-9bfd-bb23fda5150e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407850 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186377708 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407851 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407850 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407851 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "61b825c0-1272-5e4c-b3ff-4f0f75ec0886" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407851 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407848 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407852 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407851 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407852 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "80843e02-eff6-534a-9c80-13ab1c07a9fb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407852 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407847 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407853 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407854 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407853 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "dd8e3137-e924-50eb-b2e3-83c1445d70ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407853 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407846 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407854 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e8e33d31-3246-51ca-a270-794ee881c78b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407854 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407849 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186428460 #edb/ref 1030 0.6666666666666666 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186428460 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account multivariable: 2 rises / 3 eligible passed source activities = 0.666667; ne